# This repo is PUBLIC, because GitHub Pages on a free account requires it.
# Only what the site itself serves belongs here.
#
# The internal docs are deliberately excluded, not forgotten. The design log
# quotes the client's own candid feedback verbatim and contains a frame-by-frame
# teardown of another product's video assets, including its storage URLs. None
# of that should sit on a public URL under anyone's name. Keep them local, or
# put them in a separate PRIVATE repo if history is wanted.
CONTEXT.md
docs/
tools/
assets-monogram-mask.png

# Derived for the claude.ai preview link, not served by this host.
artifact.html

# Local screenshots from tools/shoot.sh and tools/check-opener.py
shot-*.png
opener-*.png

.DS_Store

# The build notes reference a private claude.ai preview link and the file's
# reformatting history. Not for a public repo. Kept local.
README.md

# Tickets derived from the spec. Same reason as the docs above: they quote the
# client and describe the reference product. Keep them local until the repo is
# private (ticket 01).
.scratch/

# The couple's supplied media. GitHub Pages serves only what is committed, so
# the ten files index.html actually requests are tracked and nothing else is:
# the source masters under assets/src/ (~57MB) and the pipeline's own notes
# (MANIFEST.md, .build-stamp.json, dress-ground.json) stay local. Note the
# glob is assets/* and not assets/ — git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, so the negations below would never be read.
assets/*
!assets/dress.jpg
!assets/garland.png
!assets/hero.mp4
!assets/manifest.json
!assets/music.m4a
!assets/opener-poster.jpg
!assets/opener-wide-poster.jpg
!assets/opener.mp4
!assets/opener-wide.mp4
!assets/venue.jpg

# Preview copies written beside index.html by tools/shoot.sh and contrast.py
# so that sibling assets resolve over file://. Removed on exit.
.preview-*.html
